WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.760
We ask a lot of questions
about our diet.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.080
What’s the right way to
treat a chronic illness?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.720
Fight off a virus,
lose weight?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.640
The problem is, we get
a lot of different answers.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.880
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.520
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.760
Today we look at
why hair turns gray,

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.840
what’s the role of genetics,
and what we can do about it.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.480
The graying of hair is one of
the most obvious signs of aging.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.760
It's also known by a technical
term that I had never heard of,

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.200
"canities."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.680
The first time I saw the word,
I misread it,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.320
wondering what gray hair
had to do with dentistry.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.640
Evidently, gray hair
isn't really white,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.520
but the pale yellowish tinge

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.200
of the constitutive
keratin protein,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.680
but, like polar bears,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.720
it just looks white by the way
light reflects off of it.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.360
Why is hair pigmented
in the first place?

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.960
Some suggest it may be
for detoxification,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.840
as natural toxins
like heavy metals

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.960
bind to the pigment melanin
to be excreted from the body

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.880
through hair outgrowth.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.800
That's why you can estimate
the amount of fish consumption

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.200
from the mercury content
of children's hair clippings,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.800
why "[a]nalysis of hair mercury

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.080
may be warranted
before pregnancy"

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.160
in women who eat a lot of fish,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.960
and why the levels
of mercury in the hair

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.840
of those eating plant-based
diets were found to be

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:33.920
up to ten times lower than those
who just occasionally ate fish.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.440
Within three months of switching
to a plant-based diet,

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:40.200
the levels of mercury, lead, and
cadmium growing out in your hair

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.440
appear to drop significantly

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.720
but build back up
when meat and eggs

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.120
are added back into the diet.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.000
Enough with the science trivia.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.800
What causes our hair
to turn gray,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.800
and what can we do about it?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.520
In medical school,
you learn about

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.520
the so-called 50-50-50 rule.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.200
By the age of 50,
the dictum goes,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.800
50 percent of the population

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.640
has at least 50 percent
gray hair.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.640
But that was based on
a homogenous population

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.840
of largely white,
fair-haired Australians.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.080
The global range is more like
6 percent to 23 percent

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.280
are 50 percent gray by 50.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.760
Though not as memorable
an axiom,

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:25.960
it looks like 75 percent or so
of people 45 to 65 years old

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.560
have about 25 percent gray hair.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.880
Those of African
or Asian descent

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.600
tend to show less gray hair.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.040
White people generally start
to gray in their mid-30s,

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.680
Asians in their late 30s,

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.360
and Africans in their mid-40s,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.080
such that premature graying
is defined

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.400
before 20 in Caucasians

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.880
but before 30
in African Americans.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:54.520
Age 25 has been suggested
as a cutoff for India.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.000
Premature or not,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.840
what causes hair to turn gray
in the first place?

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.000
The hair follicle is
a complex little mini-organ

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.040
that anchors and grows
a single hair.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.680
In the base of the follicle bulb

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.400
as few as 100
pigment-making cells

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.680
normally stain the emerging hair
shaft with melanin pigments

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.240
that can range in color
from black to red.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.560
A single hair grows for about
3.5 years before falling out

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.880
and a new one starts
growing in its place.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.760
So, graying may start
after about 10 hair cycles

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.840
when pigment deposition declines
as the pigment generating cells,

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.640
called melanocytes,
start to become depleted.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.560
What kills them off?

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.120
There's a depigmentation
disorder called vitiligo

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.480
where melanocytes
in the skin are killed off

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.480
by the buildup
of hydrogen peroxide,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.640
which can decompose
into toxic free radicals.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.600
So, researchers checked,
and indeed,

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.240
the same "massive" levels were
found in aging hair follicles.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.800
Where does the hydrogen peroxide
come from?

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:10.520
It's naturally generated as a
by-product of melanin synthesis,

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.200
but normally countered
by an antioxidant enzyme

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.880
called catalase.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:18.040
The problem, it seems,
is that catalase

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:22.000
and other antioxidant defenses
may decline as we age

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.240
and leave melanocytes vulnerable

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.160
to their own hot potato
production of pigment.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:33.040
Our own eyelashes present
"an enigma in plain sight."

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.840
Eyelashes tend to be the
darkest hairs on the human body

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.400
and undergo graying
significantly later

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.000
than other hairs.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.520
The explanation appears to be

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.880
the presence of a particular
antioxidant protein

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.920
missing from regular hair,

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.400
consistent with the prevailing

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.720
"free radical
theory of graying."

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.360
Did you know that
vitamin B12 deficiency

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.000
is one of the rare reversible
causes of hair graying?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.840
Here’s the story.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.360
The graying of hair,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.040
the age-related "exhaustion
of the pigmentary potential"

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.360
is thought to be mainly genetic,

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.760
with a family history
of premature graying

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.840
present in up to 90 percent
of cases.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.568
But if the rate of graying
is caused by oxidative damage,

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.960
what role might be played
by antioxidants

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.200
and systemic oxidative stress

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.800
outside of the hair follicle?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.960
Those with premature graying
do seem to have

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.520
higher circulating markers
of oxidative damage

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.400
and lower antioxidant levels
in blood.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.080
The higher prevalence of
premature graying among smokers

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.240
also supports this possibility
that exogenous free radicals

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.320
may speed up the accumulation
of oxidative insults

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.400
in the aging hair follicle.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.080
Obese individuals
also tend to gray early,

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.200
consistent with
the oxidative stress concept,

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.320
though drinkers do not.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.960
Alcohol consumption clearly
causes oxidative stress

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.320
yet is not
significantly associated

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.240
with premature graying.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.760
Those trying to maximize
their intake of antioxidants

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.440
by eating plant-based

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.920
must deal with
the Achilles heel-

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:14.440
the risk of
vitamin B12 deficiency

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.760
for those not actively
supplementing their diets

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.160
with B12,

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.640
whether from supplements
or fortified foods.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.000
B12 deficiency is one
of the rare reversible causes

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.240
of hair graying through
some unknown mechanism.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:32.760
Thankfully, hair can repigment
after B12 repletion.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.680
Another reversible cause
is hypothyroidism,

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:40.320
which can be reversed with
thyroid hormone replacement.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.760
Rather than oxidative stress,
what about regular stress?

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:48.080
Does fight-or-flight
turn hair white?

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.520
Marie Antoinette syndrome

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:55.080
refers to the rapid graying of
hair due to stress or trauma,

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.320
based on the (likely apocryphal)
story of her hair going

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.080
completely white
on the eve of her beheading.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.920
Sporadic validated reports
of sudden graying

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.040
have been attributed
to the sudden diffuse loss

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.600
of pigmented hairs,

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.720
leaving the gray hairs behind,

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:16.200
offering the illusion
of transmogrification.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.200
In mice, acute stressors
can lead to hair graying

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.918
via rapid depletion
of melanocyte stem cells,

00:07:22.918 --> 00:07:25.320
perhaps because
psychological stress

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.600
may lead to oxidative stress

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.280
(based on cross-sectional
studies that link higher

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:35.160
perceived stress to higher
levels of oxidative DNA damage).

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.960
Why might we even have evolved

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.760
to turn gray
in response to stress?

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.800
Drawing on an analogy
from the authority afforded

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.160
silverback mountain gorillas,

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.320
stress-induced graying
may confer

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.560
a "school of hard knocks"
evolutionary advantage

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.080
for leadership.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.720
For real-world consequences,

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.320
check out the results
of this study:

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.480
hospitalized patients

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.640
treated by gray-haired
attending physicians

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.680
were found to be
significantly more likely

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.600
to make it
out of the hospital alive

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.960
than those attended
by dark or blond-haired docs.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:15.160
As a mark of age, gray hair may
also be a mark of experience.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.680
But might having
gray hair yourself

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.880
increase your own chances
of ending up in the hospital?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.880
Might premature
or extensive graying

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:27.120
be a sign of accelerated aging

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.440
and subsequent risk
of age-related diseases?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.320
The data is mixed.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.760
Some studies suggest
the degree of graying

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:39.480
is an independent risk factor
for coronary artery disease,

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.760
for example based on higher
coronary calcium scores

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.920
in grayer individuals.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.880
However,
by far the largest study,

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.160
which followed 13,000
men and women for 16 years,

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.120
found no correlation
between graying

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.640
(or hair loss or wrinkles)

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.600
and overall mortality.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.840
The only exception appeared
to be a small fraction of men

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.320
without any gray hair

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:04.240
(just 6 percent
of those in their 50s,

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.160
2 percent of those in their 60s,

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.760
and 1 percent
of those in their 70s),

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:13.680
who did seem to have a
significantly lower mortality.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.000
